From 5e6f97361b9e6f4a9a2c96f16785a1917bec98cb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: James Trotter <james@jamesat.dev>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 01:47:44 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] channels: creator grace (channels.creator-grace)

When an unregistered channel empties, remember the account that created it
for channels.creator-grace (default 0: off). Until then only that account
gets operator status in the channel: whoever else re-creates it by joining
first doesn't (so auto-register doesn't register it to them either), and the
creator gets +o back whenever it rejoins. Guests aren't remembered. A window
is renewed only if the creator was back in the channel since it began, so
someone else re-creating and leaving can't stretch it. In memory only.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
